    },
    {
      "id": "lit4wgs",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Periodic Trends"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zl7ujkl",
      "content": "• Atomic size decreases across a period."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u37paxi",
      "content": "• Atomic size increases down a group."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f9lqfal",
      "content": "• Metallic character decreases across a period."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9kk81xl",
      "content": "• Electronegativity increases across a period."
    },
    {
      "id": "7o5vw73",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Importance of Periodic Table"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vt91xp6",
      "content": "• Helps understand properties of elements."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Mendeleev's Periodic Table was based on Atomic Mass, whereas the Modern Periodic Table is based on Atomic Number.",
        "In Dobereiner's Triads, the atomic mass of the middle element is approximately the average of the atomic masses of the other two elements.",
        "Modern Periodic Table consists of 18 vertical columns (groups) and 7 horizontal rows (periods)."
      ],
      "id": "zeny7ok"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7kyerhb",
      "content": "• Predicts properties of undiscovered elements."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rfnjapy",
      "content": "• Helps classify elements into groups."
    },
    {
      "id": "jg96ohl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r2ghwf2",
      "content": "• Mendeleev is called the Father of Periodic Table."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tvnruhq",
      "content": "• Modern periodic table is based on atomic number."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bap5xq7",
      "content": "• There are 7 periods and 18 groups."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i44e11n",
      "content": "• Noble gases belong to group 18."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}